\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces Edge deployment pipeline. (1) Sensing: the model consumes only capacity measurements ($c_t$, plus a cycle counter) from the battery. (2) The last $W{=}64$ cycles are patch-embedded to 32 tokens at $d{=}64$ ($=d_{\text  {model}}$). (3) Quantization: dynamic INT8 reduces weights from 1.3\,MB to 340\,KB ($-75\%$) with AE 2.2$\to $2.3 (lossless). (4) On-board inference in C: two GDN-2 layers with a fixed 8\,KB state per layer (16\,KB total, zero dynamic allocation) updated incrementally per cycle. (5) Fused last-token readout predicts $\hat  {c}_{t+1}$ in one step. (6) The P2.5/P50/P97.5 outputs drive calibrated RUL decisions at 8--12\,ms per inference on STM32F4 (168\,MHz).}}{29}{figure.caption.23}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:deploy}{{13}{29}{Edge deployment pipeline. (1) Sensing: the model consumes only capacity measurements ($c_t$, plus a cycle counter) from the battery. (2) The last $W{=}64$ cycles are patch-embedded to 32 tokens at $d{=}64$ ($=d_{\text {model}}$). (3) Quantization: dynamic INT8 reduces weights from 1.3\,MB to 340\,KB ($-75\%$) with AE 2.2$\to $2.3 (lossless). (4) On-board inference in C: two GDN-2 layers with a fixed 8\,KB state per layer (16\,KB total, zero dynamic allocation) updated incrementally per cycle. (5) Fused last-token readout predicts $\hat {c}_{t+1}$ in one step. (6) The P2.5/P50/P97.5 outputs drive calibrated RUL decisions at 8--12\,ms per inference on STM32F4 (168\,MHz)}{figure.caption.23}{}}
